    "result_text": "Done. The full suite (3 tests, the only concrete test class) is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented optional, city-region-validated `postcode` support for owners across the OfficeFloor create/update pipelines.\n\n**Contract & persistence**\n- `openapi.yml` \u2014 added an optional `postcode` property to `OwnerFields` (string, 4 digits, `^[0-9]{4}$`), so the generated `OwnerFieldsDto`/`OwnerDto` carry it. Left out of the `required` list to stay backward-compatible.\n- `Owner.java` \u2014 added the `postcode` field + getter/setter with `@Column(name = \"postcode\")`.\n- `db/{hsqldb,h2,mysql,postgres}/schema.sql` \u2014 added a `postcode` column to the `owners` table.\n\n**Validation (400 when present-and-invalid)**\n- `CityRegion.java` \u2014 added `postcodeRange(city)` returning the region's inclusive `{low,high}` range (NSW 2000-2099, VIC 3000-3099, QLD 4000-4099) or `null` for a city with no known region.\n- New `ValidateOwnerPostcode` function \u2014 no-op when postcode is absent/blank; else requires exactly 4 digits and, when the city's region is known, requires the value in range; a city with no known region accepts any 4-digit code.\n- New checked `InvalidPostcodeException` + `InvalidPostcodeExceptionHandler` (responds 400 with a `ProblemDetail`) + its `officefloor/escalation/\u2026InvalidPostcodeException.yml`.\n\n**Wiring**\n- `owners.POST.yml` and `owners/{ownerId}.PUT.yml` \u2014 inserted `validatePostcode` right after the body-validation step (so an invalid postcode is a 400 before build/load).\n- `ApplyOwner` \u2014 copies `postcode` on update; create maps it automatically via MapStruct (it stays in the read path too, so it's stored and returned).\n\nThe three acceptance tests (valid postcode stored/returned, absent postcode accepted, malformed `\"12\"` rejected 400) all pass.",
